A MESSAGE FROM THE GENERAL MANAGER
----------------------------------
We are pleased to present this year's Annual Water Quality Report. In 2024
your water met or surpassed every federal and state drinking water standard.
{{ ww_org_name }} is a regional wholesale supplier. We treat water from the
Cedar River and deliver it through the Cedar Ridge Regional Transmission
System to our four member communities: the City of Cedar Ridge, the Town of
Millbrook, the Village of Ashby and Harlan Township. Each member community
also publishes its own report covering its local distribution system.

                                         - Gregory Lindqvist, General Manager

WHERE DOES MY WATER COME FROM?
------------------------------
Source: Cedar River (surface water), drawn at the Cedar River Intake Pump
Station (PS-1), approximately 3.5 miles upstream of the Cedar Ridge water
treatment plant. A Source Water Assessment completed by the state in 2017
rated the Cedar River as MODERATELY susceptible to contamination, chiefly from
agricultural runoff, upstream wastewater discharges and road crossings. A copy
of the assessment is available at our office, 410 Riverside Dr, Cedar Ridge.

HOW IS MY WATER TREATED?
------------------------
The Cedar Ridge Water Treatment Plant (rated capacity 9.0 MGD) uses
conventional treatment: coagulation, flocculation, sedimentation, dual-media
filtration, chlorine disinfection, and pH adjustment with sodium hydroxide
(caustic soda) to reduce the corrosivity of the water. Finished water is
pumped through a 16-inch transmission main to the Hilltop Booster Pump
Station (PS-3) and the 1.0-million-gallon Summit Elevated Tank.

  2024 average day demand ............ 4.6 million gallons per day (MGD)
  2024 peak day demand ............... 7.9 MGD (July 18, 2024)
  Total water delivered .............. 1,684 million gallons

